module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.juxtaposed_bare_value_lowers_to_the_last_at_v2_body_lowering

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }

data juxtaposed_bare_value_lowers_to_the_last_at_v2_body_lowering: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "juxtaposed_bare_value_lowers_to_the_last_at_v2_body_lowering" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: AtCeiling { rung: StructurallyGuaranteed, ceiling_reason: "structurally guaranteed once a body's statement sequence is read by the statement authority, which refuses a non-final bare value located." as NonEmptyStr } },

  receipts: [
    "**a function body whose statement sequence leaves a non-final bare value lowers to the LAST value, and normalize ACCEPTS the module** (INVALID STATE: a body of two bracketed list literals written one under the other -- `[a, b, c]` then `[d, e]` -- lowers to `[d, e]`. The first literal is gone and there is no diagnostic. A juxtaposed bracketed literal is not an append, but reads as one.) The author wrote an enumeration and got a shorter one; a name that lived only in the dropped literal never reaches resolve, and the value the body denotes is not the value the statements compute.",
    "WHERE, cited by symbol, and the earliest unjustified boundary is LOWERING, not the grammar. The grammar correctly makes a bracketed literal on the next line a new STATEMENT and not an index suffix (`v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_grammar_index_lbracket_head_expr`, pinned by `v2.test.claim.parse.index_suffix`), so a body holding a sequence of statements is a legitimate parse. `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_try_statement_spine` reaches the refusing authority only through `body_lower_find_captured` on `dag_surface_stmt_seq` plus `body_lower_stmt_spine_has_successor`; when the juxtaposed pair is not recognised as a spine with a successor it falls through to the expression readers (`body_lower_body_subtree_lower_rest`), which read one literal and drop the other. The authority that already refuses this, `body_lower_stmt_spine` with `body_lowering_reason_statement_precedes_without_binding`, is never reached. This is a first-match/fall-through reader of the same family as `match_arm_statement_body_lowers_to_its_first_expression_at_v2_body_lowering` and `unrecognized_primary_expression_lowers_to_its_first_atom_at_v2_body_lowering`, differing only in which literal survives (the last, not the first).",
    "RECEIPTS. The dispatcher receipt is gunb-ai/gunbc #16148: at the restore base, `gunbc.harness.harness_tool_kind` `all_harness_tools` was the five core tools as the first list and the three shell-job tools as a juxtaposed second list, so `harness_tool_of_wire_name` folded only the last list -- `wait`, `job_output`, `job_kill` were recognized and `run_command`, `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `validate_worktree` came back `HarnessToolUnrecognized`; the two red rows are `each_harness_tool_wire_name_reads_back_as_its_own_tool` and `each_harness_tool_item_kind_reads_back_as_its_own_tool`. Executed by quick-newt-573 at origin/main 85758c1ab612: `all_harness_tools_len` returned 3 and the value was `[WaitJobsTool, ReadJobOutputTool, KillJobTool]` -- the last list; a probe body `[1, 2, 3]` then `[4, 5]` returned `[4, 5]`, length 2, and v2 `normalize_census` returned ACCEPTED. #16148 repairs that one instance; this row removes the class. DISTINGUISHING FACTS: not the index suffix (a next-line `[` is a statement, not an index); not `match_arm_statement_body_lowers_to_its_first_expression_at_v2_body_lowering` (that reads a match arm body to its FIRST expr; here an fn body reads to its LAST, and neither the arm nor the index is involved).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (silent wrongness -- the module normalizes, no diagnostic, the value is wrong). CEILING: structurally guaranteed. A body whose statements leave a non-final bare value lowers to the value its statements denote, or refuses at that statement with `body_lowering_reason_statement_precedes_without_binding`, located. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: v2 body lowering reads a function body's statement sequence through `body_lower_stmt_spine` -- the authority an fn tail and a match-arm statement body already use, which binds a let, takes the last statement as the value, and refuses any other statement that precedes another -- so the juxtaposed pair reaches that authority instead of the expression readers. The pinned refusal claim is `v2.test.claim.parse.juxtaposed_literal_statement` `juxtaposed_bare_value_lowers_to_the_last_refuses_holds`, red against the accepting fold and green after; the single-literal and let-then-tail positive controls stay green, proving the refusal is confined to a non-final bare value.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.parse.juxtaposed_literal_statement", decl_name: "juxtaposed_bare_value_lowers_to_the_last_refuses_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.parse.juxtaposed_literal_statement", decl_name: "juxtaposed_bare_names_refuse_under_the_same_reason_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.parse.juxtaposed_literal_statement", decl_name: "juxtaposed_bare_value_refusal_is_located_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.parse.juxtaposed_literal_statement", decl_name: "single_literal_body_is_accepted_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.parse.juxtaposed_literal_statement", decl_name: "let_then_tail_is_accepted_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
